WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.472 --> 00:00:20.041
The Mermaid wanted to see her family before she left.

2
00:00:21.282 --> 00:00:24.904
But when she reached her father's palace, everyone was asleep.

3
00:00:26.165 --> 00:00:27.906
She felt a great sadness.

4
00:00:27.926 --> 00:00:31.688
"I'm leaving my home forever," she thought.

5
00:00:32.884 --> 00:00:34.745
"And I can't even say good-bye."

6
00:00:36.005 --> 00:00:40.926
Then, just before dawn, she swam to the cliffs near the Prince's palace.

7
00:00:42.307 --> 00:00:46.248
The Little Mermaid could see the balcony after she crawled up on the rocks.

8
00:00:47.688 --> 00:00:50.909
Once on shore she swallowed the bitter brew.

9
00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:57.351
Suddenly she felt a horrible pain, like a sword striking her tiny body.

10
00:00:58.592 --> 00:01:03.226
As she fainted, the Little Mermaid saw her tail begin to split in two.

11
00:01:04.887 --> 00:01:08.469
When she awoke, she found herself on a velvet couch.

12
00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:11.551
Her body was covered by a cape.

13
00:01:12.812 --> 00:01:15.833
She looked up and saw the prince standing over her.

14
00:01:15.853 --> 00:01:20.056
"I found you lying on the rocks," the Prince said.

15
00:01:20.076 --> 00:01:22.897
"Who are you and where do you come from?"

16
00:01:24.258 --> 00:01:27.060
"I am your true love," she wanted to say.

17
00:01:28.348 --> 00:01:29.889
"I saved you from the sea."

18
00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:33.052
But of course she could not speak.

19
00:01:34.233 --> 00:01:37.496
So she smiled at the Prince, hoping he would understand.

20
00:01:37.516 --> 00:01:42.139
"Come now, don't be frightened," the Prince said warmly.

21
00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:46.082
But the Little Mermaid could only look at him with love.

22
00:01:46.102 --> 00:01:47.904
"What is your name?"

23
00:01:48.424 --> 00:01:48.985
he asked.

24
00:01:50.106 --> 00:01:51.367
The mermaid was silent.

25
00:01:52.808 --> 00:01:57.732
Finally he said, "I do not know why you will not speak, but you still need my aid."

26
00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:01.962
The Prince helped the Little Mermaid stand up.

27
00:02:03.824 --> 00:02:08.848
As the Sea Witch had warned, every footstep felt as if she were walking on knives.

28
00:02:10.489 --> 00:02:12.831
Yet to the Prince, she looked perfect.

29
00:02:14.132 --> 00:02:18.455
As they walked, she glided through the halls as lightly as a cloud.

30
00:02:18.475 --> 00:02:24.000
"How graceful you are," the Prince said as he led her into his rooms.

31
00:02:25.581 --> 00:02:29.124
He called his servants and ordered them to bring some clothes.

32
00:02:30.228 --> 00:02:32.629
"Dress her as an honored guest of the royal palace!"

33
00:02:33.309 --> 00:02:34.070
he commanded.

34
00:02:35.230 --> 00:02:41.093
Then he turned to her and asked softly, "Would you like to accompany me to the royal performance

35
00:02:41.133 --> 00:02:44.734
today?" The Little Mermaid nodded eagerly.

36
00:02:46.015 --> 00:02:51.877
After the servants dressed her in a blue silk dress, the Prince led her to the palace hall

37
00:02:52.197 --> 00:02:53.898
to introduce her to his parents.

38
00:02:55.218 --> 00:02:56.779
"How beautiful you are!"

39
00:02:57.379 --> 00:02:58.420
exclaimed the Queen.

40
00:02:59.644 --> 00:03:00.924
"Where do you come from?"

41
00:03:01.965 --> 00:03:04.946
But of course the Little Mermaid could not answer.

42
00:03:04.966 --> 00:03:10.367
A tall woman entered the hall to perform for the Prince and his parents.

43
00:03:11.567 --> 00:03:15.889
She sang very sweetly, and the Prince clapped his hands in delight.

44
00:03:16.929 --> 00:03:22.330
The Little Mermaid sadly thought, "I once sang even more sweetly."

45
00:03:23.651 --> 00:03:28.392
But as the Little Mermaid listened, she was surprised that she felt like dancing.

46
00:03:29.532 --> 00:03:33.873
She lifted her arms, and her graceful feet glided across the floor.

47
00:03:35.014 --> 00:03:40.095
The Little Mermaid danced so magically that she charmed everyone, especially the Prince.

48
00:03:44.516 --> 00:03:46.857
are so special," he said.

49
00:03:46.877 --> 00:03:51.298
"I will always keep you with me and call you my little companion."

50
00:03:52.438 --> 00:03:54.559
The Little Mermaid smiled up at him.

51
00:03:55.759 --> 00:03:58.700
Her eyes asked, "Is that a promise?"

52
00:04:00.256 --> 00:04:04.878
As time went on, the Little Mermaid became the Prince's best friend.

53
00:04:06.018 --> 00:04:07.758
He took her with him wherever he went.

54
00:04:08.879 --> 00:04:13.360
They walked through the royal gardens and rode through the fields on horseback.

55
00:04:14.741 --> 00:04:17.742
They climbed mountains that almost reached the sky.

56
00:04:18.902 --> 00:04:25.164
And though she could not speak to him, she kept smiling—even as her feet stung with pain.
